\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Cluster census of the compatibility graph: every connected component of every event, three events per configuration. Almost every cluster is a single isolated segment. Among those that are not, the three named families of section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:toy:graphs} account for essentially all of them, and the components carrying a cycle --- which nothing forbids --- are a fraction of a percent even at the worst corner. Percentages in the right-hand block are of the multi-segment clusters, not of all clusters.\relax }}{11}{table.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:census}{{1}{11}{Cluster census of the compatibility graph: every connected component of every event, three events per configuration. Almost every cluster is a single isolated segment. Among those that are not, the three named families of section~\ref {sec:toy:graphs} account for essentially all of them, and the components carrying a cycle --- which nothing forbids --- are a fraction of a percent even at the worst corner. Percentages in the right-hand block are of the multi-segment clusters, not of all clusters.\relax }{table.caption.5}{}}
