\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The three filters of one lineage, drawn to the same conventions. (a) HHL: prepare $|b\rangle $, estimate each eigenvalue into an $n_c$-qubit clock, rotate the flag by $2\qopname  \relax o{arcsin}(C/\tilde  \lambda )$ conditioned on the clock value, uncompute, post-select the flag. (b) The one-bit quantum filter: the same structure with a one-qubit clock, the rotation replaced by a NOT on the flag conditioned on the clock reading $|0\rangle $, and the uniform state as input; the states $|\Psi _1\rangle $--$|\Psi _4\rangle $ are eqs.\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:psi1}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}--\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:psi4}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}. (c) The QSVT of section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:qsvt}: an index register prepared in the coefficient amplitudes controls powers of the qubitization walk $W$ on the dilation and system registers; unpreparing and post-selecting both ancillary registers on zero applies the Chebyshev series $p(X)$. Wires carrying several qubits are marked with their count. The 1BQF as drawn is the correct one-bit filter; the circuit as built in the package realises the evolution as a per-pair product (section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:fork:trotter}).\relax }}{20}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:circuits}{{9}{20}{The three filters of one lineage, drawn to the same conventions. (a) HHL: prepare $|b\rangle $, estimate each eigenvalue into an $n_c$-qubit clock, rotate the flag by $2\arcsin (C/\tilde \lambda )$ conditioned on the clock value, uncompute, post-select the flag. (b) The one-bit quantum filter: the same structure with a one-qubit clock, the rotation replaced by a NOT on the flag conditioned on the clock reading $|0\rangle $, and the uniform state as input; the states $|\Psi _1\rangle $--$|\Psi _4\rangle $ are eqs.~\eqref {eq:psi1}--\eqref {eq:psi4}. (c) The QSVT of section~\ref {sec:qsvt}: an index register prepared in the coefficient amplitudes controls powers of the qubitization walk $W$ on the dilation and system registers; unpreparing and post-selecting both ancillary registers on zero applies the Chebyshev series $p(X)$. Wires carrying several qubits are marked with their count. The 1BQF as drawn is the correct one-bit filter; the circuit as built in the package realises the evolution as a per-pair product (section~\ref {sec:fork:trotter}).\relax }{figure.caption.14}{}}
\citation{trackhhl}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces The two response functions against the populated spectrum ($s=4$). (a) The 1BQF cosine: one zero, placed on the isolated-false line; the bright lines of the coupled false motifs (pair, triple) sit on the slopes and pass. (b) The degree-40 line comb: passes at the four true-track lines only, with the isolated, pair and triple lines all rejected.\relax }}{21}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
