\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces The threshold trade-off, on the stored $T=400$ clean event of the canonical campaign: (a) segment efficiency and (b) segment false rate as the threshold $\tau $ sweeps, for the classical solver, the 1BQF (package circuit, as stored) and the QSVT (degree 40, base $A$). The quantum amplitudes are placed on the classical scale by norm-matching on the classical solver's own efficiency-first support. The dashed verticals are each solver's efficiency-first working point (the lowest threshold keeping 99\% of its true segments); the QSVT holds both high efficiency and a $\sim 10^{-2}$ false rate over the whole usable range.\relax }}{24}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:threshold}{{13}{24}{The threshold trade-off, on the stored $T=400$ clean event of the canonical campaign: (a) segment efficiency and (b) segment false rate as the threshold $\tau $ sweeps, for the classical solver, the 1BQF (package circuit, as stored) and the QSVT (degree 40, base $A$). The quantum amplitudes are placed on the classical scale by norm-matching on the classical solver's own efficiency-first support. The dashed verticals are each solver's efficiency-first working point (the lowest threshold keeping 99\% of its true segments); the QSVT holds both high efficiency and a $\sim 10^{-2}$ false rate over the whole usable range.\relax }{figure.caption.18}{}}
