\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {25}{\ignorespaces The same scan on heavy noise. The efficiency curves are sigmoids in $\qopname  \relax o{log}d$ whose onset degree is set by the operator: the fork rises first ($0.91$ by $d{=}16$), base $A$ next ($d{\approx }20$), the occupancy operators last ($d\gtrsim 64$), because the co-hit term widens the spectral domain and a fixed degree loses resolution proportionally (the span wall of section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:atscale:density}). The 1BQF stars sit at zero for every operator here.\relax }}{43}{figure.caption.31}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:degheavy}{{25}{43}{The same scan on heavy noise. The efficiency curves are sigmoids in $\log d$ whose onset degree is set by the operator: the fork rises first ($0.91$ by $d{=}16$), base $A$ next ($d{\approx }20$), the occupancy operators last ($d\gtrsim 64$), because the co-hit term widens the spectral domain and a fixed degree loses resolution proportionally (the span wall of section~\ref {sec:atscale:density}). The 1BQF stars sit at zero for every operator here.\relax }{figure.caption.31}{}}
