\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {28}{\ignorespaces Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:responses}'s question asked of the fitted responses: $|p(\lambda )|$ per operator (rep-0 universal response, moderate noise) against that operator's exact motif lines. The fork system's response concentrates into a single dominant pass — the term has simplified the spectrum the fit must explain. The occupancy responses live on a span-widened domain (insets; the motif window is the shaded sliver), so their $d{=}80$ passes are visibly coarser inside it — the resolution cost $\mathrm  {span}/d$ paid for breaking the twins.\relax }}{46}{figure.caption.34}\protected@file@percent }
